From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Aldea <andrei1998@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 10:53:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] video: add SSD16xx e-paper display support

Add damage-aware synchronization and a data-driven SPI video driver
for Solomon Systech SSD16xx e-paper controllers. Initial support covers
the Good Display GDEY042T81 400x300 panel with an SSD1683.

Convert RGB565 pixels to monochrome, use nonblocking refreshes, and
periodically force a full refresh to limit ghosting. Quiesce the panel
before handing its SPI and GPIO resources to the operating system.

Add sandbox coverage for synchronization, conversion, error handling,
refresh cadence, and shutdown.

Keep driver synchronization unconditional by default and make rate limiting
an explicit capability for slow-transfer drivers such as SSD16xx.

The panel sequence is derived from Texas Instruments Linux revision
7845a75c5c754570830696603142090002afbe14. Texas Instruments granted
permission to distribute this port under GPL-2.0-or-later.

Developed with assistance from OpenAI Codex.

Link: https://github.com/TexasInstruments/ti-linux-kernel/commit/7845a75c5c754570830696603142090002afbe14
Signed-off-by: Andrei Aldea <andrei1998@gmail.com>
